  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 028dec5536905af45ba56d38d954a849, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SimpleXRHoverInfo
  objectName: Jellyfish
  description: Jellyfish are mesmerizing, gelatinous marine creatures that have drifted
    through the world's oceans for over 500 million years, making them even older
    than dinosaurs. Remarkably simple in their biology, they lack a brain, heart,
    bones, and blood; instead, their elegant, bell-shaped bodies are composed of
    about 95% water. They navigate the seas through a combination of rhythmic pulsing
    and drifting along ocean currents. Jellyfish are most famous for their trailing
    tentacles, which are armed with thousands of specialized stinging cells called
    nematocysts, used primarily to stun and capture prey like plankton and small
    fish. Ranging in size from smaller than a pinhead to massive giants with tentacles
    stretching over 100 feet, these ethereal predators add a beautiful but formidable
    presence to coral reefs and open waters alike.
  objectInfoCanvas: {fileID: 626478486}
  infoPanel: {fileID: 1365102933}
  infoText: {fileID: 496564549}
  progressCircle: {fileID: 1459134083}
  progressImage: {fileID: 1459134085}
  showDelay: 3
